{{- /*
  The page every other host gets: a customer's site, a custom domain, anything
  the platform hosts for somebody else. It says whose it is by saying nothing:
  no mark, no name, no link, no brand colour. Its visitor has never heard of
  the platform underneath, and a notice about the platform on their shopfront
  would put someone else's name on their outage. errorpages.go says why.

  Self-contained for the same reason the branded page is: one inline
  stylesheet, no font file, no script, no image.
*/ -}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" content="#f7f7f5">
<meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" content="#07090a">
<title>{{.Title}}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{.Message}}">
<style>
/*
  The neutrals of the platform palette and none of its accent. They are
  copied rather than imported because a page that may fetch nothing cannot
  import anything, and errorpages_test.go fails the build when they drift from
  the brand tokens. A plain light set plus a dark override, not light-dark(),
  so that an older browser still gets its colours.
*/
:root {
  --bg: #f7f7f5;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --fg: #191d1a;
  --muted: #5b615c;
  --line: #e5e6e2;
  color-scheme: light dark;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --bg: #07090a;
    --surface: #0b1110;
    --fg: #e8e6dd;
    --muted: #9ca395;
    --line: #18231e;
  }
}

*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }

body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 1.5rem;
  min-height: 100vh;
  min-height: 100dvh;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--fg);
  font-family: "InterVariable", "Inter", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

main {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 26rem;
  padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
  text-align: center;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 0.625rem;
}

h1 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.35;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
p {
  margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>{{.Heading}}</h1>
<p>{{.Detail}}</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
